---
title: "One sticky note: typing, saving, outside edits, conflict versions, archive and Trash"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: syncing
    lg1: stored
    lg2: Breaks CloseAlwaysWorks or TypedTextKept
    lg3: Breaks NoSpuriousConflictBlock or WindowMatchesDisk in some cases
    lg4: Path to the CloseAlwaysWorks or NoSpuriousConflictBlock or TypedTextKept or WindowMatchesDisk bug
    state "Terms" as terms {
      direction TB
      state " " as tc0 {
        direction LR
        tm0: person = The owner, using Sticky Notes on this Mac.
        tm1: save timer = The half-second pause after typing before the note is written to its file.
        tm2: file watcher = The part of the app that notices the note's file changed on disk.
        tm3: desk = The app part that keeps one window per active note.
      }
      state " " as tc1 {
        direction LR
        tm4: outside edit = A change to the note's file made by Obsidian, the other Mac or iCloud.
        tm5: conflict version = A second copy of the file that iCloud keeps when two saves disagree.
        tm6: conflict sweep = The app step that merges conflict versions back into the file.
        tm7: other Mac = The owner's second Mac, used in turn, not at the same time.
      }
      state " " as tc2 {
        direction LR
        tm8: Obsidian = The notes app that shares the vault folder.
        tm9: iCloud = iCloud Drive, which syncs the vault between the Macs.
        tm10: placeholder = A hidden stand-in file iCloud leaves for a file it has not downloaded.
        tm11: archive = Closed notes, still listed in the notes panel.
      }
      state " " as tc3 {
        direction LR
        tm12: Trash = Notes deleted from the archive, kept 30 days.
      }
    }
  }
  class lg0 orange
  class lg1 teal
  class lg2 breaks
  class lg3 mayBreak
  class lg4 bugPath
  s0: New note, no file yet
  s1: New note with text, not written yet
  s2: File changed, window not told yet
  s3: No note file, window closed
  s4: Typing, save pending
  s5: Save pending, person in another window
  s6: Disk not accepting writes, note open
  s7: Outside edit held back
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: the person types in the note
  s1 --> s2: the half-second save timer writes the note
  s1 --> s1: the disk stops accepting writes
  s2 --> s4: the person types in the note
  s1 --> s3: the person clicks the note's close button
  s4 --> s5: the person switches to another window
  s4 --> s6: the disk stops accepting writes
  s5 --> s5: the file watcher reports the change to the window [the window shows it]
  s6 --> s6: the half-second save timer writes the note or the file watcher reports the change to the window [the window holds it back] or the person types in the note or the person switches to another window
  s5 --> s6: the disk stops accepting writes
  s6 --> s7: the disk accepts writes again
  classDef breaks fill:#ffecee,stroke:#e72e3b,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#cd2834
  classDef mayBreak fill:#fff3e6,stroke:#e8730c,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#b85a06
  class s0 teal
  class s0 bugPath
  class s1 teal
  class s1 bugPath
  class s2 orange
  class s2 bugPath
  class s3 teal
  class s3 breaks
  class s3 bugPath
  class s4 orange
  class s4 bugPath
  class s5 bugPath
  class s6 mayBreak
  class s6 bugPath
  class s7 orange
  class s7 breaks
  class s7 bugPath
